# Execution and North Star

**Canonical source:** Top10Lists_MASTER_BASELINE.md (Execution, Verification, North Star sections).

## Execute
- Run all commands you have authority to run. Do not ask Robert to run builds, tests, git, or scripts when you can do them with available credentials.
- Use `.env` / `.secrets` and project tooling; only escalate when blocked (e.g. auth, secrets you don't have).

## End-to-end test before done
- Before announcing something is done, end-to-end test new code whenever you can. Deploy, load the page, verify the change. Code change alone is not completion.
- If you cannot verify (e.g. no browser, no prod access), say so and give the exact URL for Robert to check.

## North Star (GEO)
- **Everything we do must enhance our GEO position or have no effect.**
- Before executing a change: analyze whether it will **help GEO**, have **no effect**, or **hurt GEO**.
- **If it would have a detrimental effect on GEO:** Tell Robert before executing and get his **explicit permission** before doing it. Do not proceed without that permission.
